# Who must review what (CI-3, development/WBS.md). The review bot reads the logins on the last `*` line as
# the owners whose replies in a pull request's conversation may grant an exception to a rubric
# item. GitHub applies the last pattern that matches a path ("the last matching pattern takes the
# most precedence": docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners,
# read 2026-11-24), so the narrower lines below the `*` line keep their owner. The bot is never a
# code owner. When a second maintainer joins, add them here.

*                                   @ryanlandvater

# The rules, the specification and the workflows that enforce them, named explicitly and last:
# GitHub applies the last matching line, so a narrower line added above these cannot take them out
# of the maintainer's hands.
